Title: The Habitual Boredom Scale: Preliminary Findings
Abstract: This research presents the conceptualization of habitual boredom and the development of a scale to measure it. The authors distinguish habitual boredom from situational boredom and identify five overlapping psychological themes associated with habitual boredom: ambivalence, passive avoidance stance, passive hope, identity confusion, and shame. The latest version of the 35-item scale is reported to be fairly reliable, with seven items measuring each of the five themes. The findings suggest that people experiencing habitual boredom may be at risk of serious psychological impacts that are not necessarily reduced by changes in their circumstances.
Keywords: habitual boredom, situational boredom, ambivalence, passive stance, passive hope, identity confusion, shame
